WEBVTT

00:00:00.629 --> 00:00:01.470
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.850 --> 00:00:06.750
In this lesson, we cut long hair into a one-length bob, at chin length.

00:00:07.186 --> 00:00:09.710
You heard the reason for each step in the theory lesson.

00:00:10.096 --> 00:00:11.150
Here, we do it.

00:00:11.808 --> 00:00:12.602
Step one:

00:00:12.825 --> 00:00:13.722
preparation.

00:00:14.331 --> 00:00:15.402
Wash your hands.

00:00:15.486 --> 00:00:16.049
Scissors,

00:00:15.999 --> 00:00:20.602
combs and clips have all been cleaned and disinfected after the previous client.

00:00:21.107 --> 00:00:24.166
Wrap a disposable neck strip around the client's neck,

00:00:24.116 --> 00:00:26.282
and only then fasten the cape over it.

00:00:26.955 --> 00:00:27.733
Step two:

00:00:27.907 --> 00:00:30.111
the consultation, while the hair is dry,

00:00:30.061 --> 00:00:32.533
as in the consultation and sectioning lesson.

00:00:32.934 --> 00:00:37.199
Look at the reference photo, and ask whether the client often ties her hair up,

00:00:37.149 --> 00:00:38.693
or tucks it behind her ears.

00:00:38.952 --> 00:00:40.933
Agree on the length with a reference point:

00:00:41.202 --> 00:00:44.693
fold a section of hair up to the chin, and say it back to the client.

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:47.813
Look at the hairline at the nape, and look for a whorl.

00:00:48.137 --> 00:00:49.813
Look at the neck and the shoulders.

00:00:50.054 --> 00:00:53.173
If the hair is curly or wavy, say beforehand:

00:00:53.434 --> 00:00:57.173
once dry, the hair shrinks up, so we leave it a little longer.

00:00:57.810 --> 00:00:58.616
Step three:

00:00:58.865 --> 00:01:03.976
shampoo, towel-dry, and detangle from the ends up, as in the earlier lesson.

00:01:04.311 --> 00:01:07.096
The hair just needs to be evenly damp, not dripping.

00:01:07.515 --> 00:01:11.656
As you cut, the hair dries, so mist it again to keep it evenly damp.

00:01:12.085 --> 00:01:15.736
Going from long hair to a bob, a lot of length comes off.

00:01:15.974 --> 00:01:18.475
Many stylists first cut off some of the ends,

00:01:18.425 --> 00:01:21.416
leaving it a few centimeters longer than the bob line,

00:01:21.524 --> 00:01:23.016
to make it easier to work with.

00:01:23.521 --> 00:01:27.099
If the client wants to keep her hair, ask before the shampoo,

00:01:27.049 --> 00:01:28.776
tie the hair into a ponytail,

00:01:28.965 --> 00:01:30.616
and cut it while it is still dry.

00:01:31.289 --> 00:01:32.139
Step four:

00:01:32.315 --> 00:01:33.019
sectioning.

00:01:33.558 --> 00:01:36.699
Make a center parting, from the front hairline to the crown.

00:01:37.175 --> 00:01:41.259
Then divide the sections, clipping each one neatly, flat against the head.

00:01:41.764 --> 00:01:45.739
At the back, let down a very thin horizontal section at the nape.

00:01:46.088 --> 00:01:47.179
Clip all the rest up.

00:01:47.858 --> 00:01:48.786
Step five:

00:01:48.970 --> 00:01:50.306
the guideline at the nape.

00:01:50.782 --> 00:01:55.586
Have the client tip her head forward slightly, chin a little down, and hold still.

00:01:56.094 --> 00:02:00.706
Comb the section straight down, close to the neck, at 0° elevation.

00:02:01.274 --> 00:02:05.661
Hold the hair between your index and middle fingers, fingers horizontal,

00:02:05.611 --> 00:02:07.106
with very light tension.

00:02:07.691 --> 00:02:10.917
Cut a straight horizontal line, just below your fingers,

00:02:10.867 --> 00:02:13.186
with the blade parallel to your fingers.

00:02:13.425 --> 00:02:16.866
Your fingers always stay between the blade and the skin of the neck.

00:02:17.126 --> 00:02:20.545
Cut the center first, then the sides, following the center.

00:02:21.127 --> 00:02:22.407
For a chin-length bob,

00:02:22.357 --> 00:02:26.546
the line at the nape usually sits around the middle of the neck, or lower,

00:02:26.654 --> 00:02:28.066
depending on the agreed shape.

00:02:28.406 --> 00:02:30.306
Once cut, check right away:

00:02:30.497 --> 00:02:33.346
both ends level, and the line parallel to the floor.

00:02:33.993 --> 00:02:34.870
Step six:

00:02:35.048 --> 00:02:36.230
the layers at the back.

00:02:36.674 --> 00:02:40.710
Let down the next horizontal section, about one to two centimeters thick.

00:02:41.058 --> 00:02:43.350
Comb it straight down, over the guideline.

00:02:43.942 --> 00:02:47.830
Look through the thin layer of hair, and you will see the guideline underneath.

00:02:48.093 --> 00:02:49.430
Cut exactly to it.

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:51.510
No lifting, no tension.

00:02:51.975 --> 00:02:55.837
Keep going like this, layer by layer, up to the occipital bone,

00:02:55.787 --> 00:02:57.350
and then up to the crown.

00:02:57.593 --> 00:03:00.710
Keep the head in the same position until the back is finished.

00:03:01.059 --> 00:03:03.528
At the occipital bone, the head curves out,

00:03:03.478 --> 00:03:06.790
and the hair is easily pulled outward with the head shape.

00:03:07.219 --> 00:03:10.390
Comb it really straight down, close to the layer below.

00:03:10.739 --> 00:03:13.750
Lift it even slightly, and the line becomes layered.

00:03:14.098 --> 00:03:16.550
For thick hair, take even thinner layers.

00:03:17.222 --> 00:03:18.083
Step seven:

00:03:18.344 --> 00:03:19.203
the sides.

00:03:19.662 --> 00:03:24.803
Now, have the client lift her head straight again, sit up straight, legs uncrossed.

00:03:25.154 --> 00:03:27.843
Let down the lowest horizontal section by the ear.

00:03:28.195 --> 00:03:32.619
Comb it down, take a little of the already cut hair from the back as a guide,

00:03:32.569 --> 00:03:34.323
and continue the line forward,

00:03:34.425 --> 00:03:35.043
to the chin.

00:03:35.533 --> 00:03:38.483
At the ear, don't pull the hair tight over the ear.

00:03:38.621 --> 00:03:41.603
Hold it very lightly, so the hair falls naturally.

00:03:41.859 --> 00:03:44.323
Work layer by layer, up to the parting.

00:03:44.585 --> 00:03:46.643
Then do exactly the same on the other side.

00:03:47.317 --> 00:03:48.022
Step eight:

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:48.822
check.

00:03:49.355 --> 00:03:51.622
Stand behind the client, and look in the mirror.

00:03:51.957 --> 00:03:54.262
Head straight, eyes looking straight ahead.

00:03:54.594 --> 00:03:56.797
Hold the two ends on either side of the chin,

00:03:56.747 --> 00:03:58.902
and see whether they are at the same height.

00:03:59.354 --> 00:04:03.222
Whichever side is longer, trim it to match the other, a little at a time.

00:04:03.559 --> 00:04:08.902
Then comb the hair straight down, look from behind, and from the side, on each side.

00:04:09.157 --> 00:04:13.222
The line must be straight, continuous, and parallel to the floor.

00:04:13.405 --> 00:04:18.022
Where the back meets the sides, just behind the ear, there is often a small corner.

00:04:18.271 --> 00:04:20.582
Trim it lightly, so the line flows again.

00:04:21.250 --> 00:04:22.121
Step nine:

00:04:22.299 --> 00:04:24.281
blow-dry, and check when dry.

00:04:24.694 --> 00:04:27.910
Dry in the direction the hair falls, from top to bottom,

00:04:27.860 --> 00:04:30.681
with a round brush turning the ends gently under.

00:04:31.099 --> 00:04:34.841
Once dry, comb the hair straight down, and look at the line again.

00:04:35.263 --> 00:04:38.601
Any strands sticking out, trim them with the tips of the scissors.

00:04:38.861 --> 00:04:42.841
If the client wants softer ends, point cut very lightly at the ends.

00:04:43.365 --> 00:04:47.558
Before finishing, remember the three most common mistakes when cutting a bob.

00:04:48.026 --> 00:04:49.078
Mistake number one:

00:04:49.254 --> 00:04:52.678
accidentally lifting the hair a little, especially at the occipital bone.

00:04:53.027 --> 00:04:55.718
The line becomes layered, and the ends lose their weight.

00:04:56.135 --> 00:04:57.238
Mistake number two:

00:04:57.519 --> 00:04:59.318
pulling the hair tight over the ear.

00:04:59.586 --> 00:05:03.638
When you let go, the hair springs up, leaving a gap right above the ear.

00:05:04.056 --> 00:05:05.158
Mistake number three:

00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:08.518
the head is tilted, or the client crosses her legs.

00:05:08.826 --> 00:05:11.878
The two sides end up uneven, and you don't even know it.

00:05:12.219 --> 00:05:16.071
All three mistakes can be avoided with thin sections, light hands,

00:05:16.021 --> 00:05:17.798
and checking the mirror often.

00:05:18.459 --> 00:05:19.314
Step ten:

00:05:19.509 --> 00:05:20.274
the finish.

00:05:20.594 --> 00:05:22.194
Brush the loose hair off the neck.

00:05:22.370 --> 00:05:24.514
Show the client the back with a hand mirror.

00:05:24.909 --> 00:05:28.114
Ask if she would like anything adjusted, and adjust it right then.

00:05:28.691 --> 00:05:30.834
Show the client how to blow-dry it at home.

00:05:31.257 --> 00:05:33.314
Write the length you cut in the client record.

00:05:33.672 --> 00:05:38.114
Many clients come back for a trim after about six to eight weeks, to keep the line.

00:05:38.758 --> 00:05:40.124
After the client leaves:

00:05:40.161 --> 00:05:43.701
scissors, combs and clips are cleaned and disinfected,

00:05:43.651 --> 00:05:45.964
as in the lesson on cleaning tools.

00:05:46.469 --> 00:05:49.724
Throw away the neck strip, and sweep up the hair under the chair.

00:05:50.098 --> 00:05:53.084
And now, please take the short quiz below the video.
